'''''Hoheria angustifolia''''', the '''narrow-leaved lacebark''' or '''narrow-leaved houhere''', is a [[species]] of [[flowering plant]] in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] Malvaceae, [[endemism|endemic]] to New Zealand. It is an [[evergreen]] tree or shrub with a weeping habit and grows to {{convert|10|m|ft|0|abbr=on}} tall.<ref name="Native Trees">{{cite book | title=The Native Trees of New Zealand | last=Salmon| first=J.T.| year=2005 | page=183 | publisher=[[Reed Publishing]] | location=Auckland, New Zealand}}</ref><ref name="Pipipi Wilson">{{cite journal |last1=Wilson |first1=Hugh | authorlink=Hugh Wilson (New Zealand botanist) | title=White lace at Lothlorien |journal=Pīpipi |date=November 2016 |volume=44 |page=8}}</ref> Known as '''houhere''' or '''houhi''' in [[Māori language|Māori]], the bark of the tree was occasionally used for traditional textiles, similar to the traditional use of ''[[Hoheria populnea]]''.<ref>{{Cite Q|Q58677501}}</ref>

It is commonly described in literature with a [[diameter at breast height]] (DBH) of up to {{convert|30|cm}}, but botanist [[Hugh Wilson (New Zealand botanist)|Hugh Wilson]] found a specimen in [[Hinewai Reserve]] with a DBH of {{convert|130|cm}}.<ref name="Pipipi Wilson" /> It has grey-green to dark green leaves, and white flowers from December to February. It has a [[Divaricate|divaricating]] small leaved habit while young until it gets to about {{convert|2|m|ft|0|abbr=on}} high. The adult leaves are narrow and coarsely toothed hence the common name of ''narrow-leaved lacebark''.<ref>{{cite web|title=Narrow-leaved lacebark|url=http://www.teara.govt.nz/en/photograph/13819/narrow-leaved-lacebark|work=Story: Shrubs and small trees of the forest|publisher=Te Ara The Encyclopedia of New Zealand|accessdate=1 April 2013}}</ref> Distribution is larger than any of the other lacebark species and can be found mostly in the eastern [[South Island]], and in the [[North Island]] from [[Taranaki]] down.<ref name="Native Trees" />

==Etymology==
''Hoheria'' is derived from the Māori vernacular name for this [[genus]], ''houhere'' or ''hoihere''.<ref name= "gledhill">Gledhill, David (2008). "The Names of Plants". Cambridge University Press. {{ISBN|9780521866453}} (hardback), {{ISBN|9780521685535}} (paperback).  pp 49, 202</ref>

''Angustifolia'' means 'with narrow leaves'.<ref name= "gledhill" />

